      "side": 1,
      "message": "But this bit is still wrong: we should use `adr` as what we want is to check that the absolute `entry` (`x29`) was aligned, not the PC-relative one (`x30`). Asserting that `entry` is properly linked at a page-aligned address should in turn be done at build time, most probably in the linker script. As it already hard-codes the address, it seems superfluous to do such a check in the end.",
